ttps://circularmaterialsystems.com/en/\">CONCEPT</a></li><li id=\"menu-item-15\" class=\"menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-15\"><a href=\"https://circularmaterialsystems.com/en/cases/\">BUILDINGS</a></li><li id=\"menu-item-23\" class=\"menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-23\"><a href=\"https://circularmaterialsystems.com/en/practice/\">PRACTICES</a></li><li id=\"menu-item-29\" class=\"menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-29\"><a href=\"https://circularmaterialsystems.com/en/about/\">ABOUT</a></li><li id=\"menu-item-214\" class=\"trp-language-switcher-container menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-language_switcher menu-item-has-children current-language-menu-item menu-item-214\"><a href=\"https://circularmaterialsystems.com/en/case/05_ferme-du-rail/\"><span data-no-translation><span class=\"trp-ls-language-name\">EN</span></span></a><ul class=\"sub-menu\"><li id=\"menu-item-206\" class=\"trp-language-switcher-container menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-language_switcher menu-item-206\"><a href=\"https://circularmaterialsystems.com/de/case/05_ferme-du-rail/\"><span data-no-translation><span class=\"trp-ls-language-name\">DE</span></span></a></li></ul></li></ul></div></nav></div></header><div id=\"content\" class=\"site-content\"><div id=\"primary\" class=\"content-area\"><main id=\"main\" class=\"site-main\" role=\"main\"><article class=\"m-block mb-article\"><div class=\"container\"><header><h1>Ferme du Rail</h1>\n<strong>Paris, France</strong></header></div><figure class=\"m-block single-thumbnail-header\"><img data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciIHdpZHRoPSIxNTAwIiBoZWlnaHQ9IjczNyIgdmlld0JveD0iMCAwIDE1MDAgNzM3Ij48cmVjdCB3aWR0aD0iMTAwJSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxMDAlIiBzdHlsZT0iZmlsbDojY2ZkNGRiO2ZpbGwtb3BhY2l0eTogMC4xOyIvPjwvc3ZnPg==\" width=\"1500\" height=\"737\" data-src=\"https://circularmaterialsystems.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/01_fdr_banner-e1714669999952.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full wp-image-805 wp-post-image\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" fetchpriority=\"high\" data-mwl-img-id=\"805\" /></figure><div class=\"info-container\"><div class=\"infobox\"><dl><dt><span>Time</span></dt><dd><span>2014 - 2019</span></dd><dt><span>Building type</span></dt><dd><span>New Built</span></dd><dt><span>Client</span></dt><dd><span>City of Paris, Grand Paris</span></dd><dt><span>Architect</span></dt><dd><span>Grand Huit Architecture</span></dd><dt><span>Project Partners</span></dt><dd><span>Julien Virgili (structural engineer), Travail et Vie, Bail pour tous (operator), Mélanie Devret (landscape architect), Philippe Peiger (urban agro-ecologist), Pouget Consultants (thermal engineering), Albert & Compagnie (sustainability advisor), Bellastock (reuse material logistics), Frédéric Cousin (straw and air-tightness system)</span></dd><dt><span>Size</span></dt><dd><span>2300 m2 (1000 m2 built)</span></dd><dt><span>Use</span></dt><dd><span>Mixed use (farming, restaurant, housing)</span></dd><dt><span>Website</span></dt><dd><span><a href=\"https://www.fermedurail.org\" class=\"link\">Link ↗</a></span></dd><dt><span>Banner image</span></dt><dd><span></span></dd></dl></div><div class=\"tags\"><a href=\"https://circularmaterialsystems.com/en/practice/collaborating-with-all-stakeholders/\" class=\"button lined tag collaborating-with-all-stakeholders\" style=\"background-color: #ff7212; color: #ff7212; border-color: #ff7212\"><span>Collaborating with all stakeholders</span></a>\n<a href=\"https://circularmaterialsystems.com/en/practice/dynamic-design-and-planning/\" class=\"button lined tag dynamic-design-and-planning\" style=\"background-color: #4d4d4d; color: #4d4d4d; border-color: #4d4d4d\"><span>Dynamic design and planning</span></a>\n<a href=\"https://circularmaterialsystems.com/en/practice/extending-the-metabolism/\" class=\"button lined tag extending-the-metabolism\" style=\"background-color: #4d4d4d; color: #4d4d4d; border-color: #4d4d4d\"><span>Extending the metabolism</span></a>\n<a href=\"https://circularmaterialsystems.com/en/practice/designing-for-modularity/\" class=\"button lined tag designing-for-modularity\" style=\"background-color: #4d4d4d; color: #4d4d4d; border-color: #4d4d4d\"><span>Designing for modularity</span></a>\n<a href=\"https://circularmaterialsystems.com/en/practice/material-based/\" class=\"button lined tag material-based\" style=\"background-color: #4d4d4d; color: #4d4d4d; border-color: #4d4d4d\"><span>Designing material-based</span></a>\n<a href=\"https://circularmaterialsystems.com/en/practice/using-natural-materials/\" class=\"button lined tag using-natural-materials\" style=\"background-color: #2d9e40; color: #2d9e40; border-color: #2d9e40\"><span>Using natural materials</span></a>\n<a href=\"https://circularmaterialsystems.com/en/practice/reuse-recycle/\" class=\"button lined tag reuse-recycle\" style=\"background-color: #2d9e40; color: #2d9e40; border-color: #2d9e40\"><span>Using reused and recycled materials</span></a></div></div><div class=\"sectional-content\"><h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">General description</h3><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Ferme du Rail was designed as an urban farm, responding to the 2014 call for entries <em>Réinventer Paris</em>. Connected to the <em>Petite Ceinture</em>, a disaffected railway running through Paris, it is a place where urban agriculture and social integration unfold. One building houses fifteen disadvantaged people and people from marginalised communities as well as five horticulture students. The other building contains a greenhouse and a restaurant. The goal is to integrate socially excluded people into a community through agricultural work and by running the restaurant.</p><figure class=\"wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped wp-block-gallery-1 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex\"><figure class=