\"><div class=\"display-table-cell vertical-align-middle breadcrumb text-small alt-font\"><ul class=\"pofo-single-post-title-breadcrumb-single page-title-style-9 \"><li class=\"text-dark-gray\">23 Jun 2025</li><li><span class=\"text-dark-gray\">By <a href=\"https://timberdevelopment.uk/author/mattmilton/\" class=\"text-dark-gray\">Matt Milton</a></span></li></ul></div></div></div></div></section><div id=\"post-46203\" class=\"post-46203 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-design tag-heyne-tillett-steel tag-hybrid tag-stora-enso-uk-ltd\"><div class=\"pofo-rich-snippet display-none\"><span class=\"entry-title\">The Print and Ink buildings: a two-edition set for Timber Square</span><span class=\"author vcard\"><a class=\"url fn n\" href=\"https://timberdevelopment.uk/author/mattmilton/\">Matt Milton</a></span><span class=\"published\">23 June 25</span><time class=\"updated\" datetime=\"2025-06-23T13:57:45+01:00\">23 June 25</time></div><section class=\"single-post-main-section\"><div class=\"container pofo_layout_right_sidebar_single\"><div class=\"row\"><div class=\"col-md-9 col-sm-12 col-xs-12 padding-45px-right no-padding-left sm-no-padding-lr sm-margin-60px-bottom xs-margin-40px-bottom\"><div class=\"col-md-12 col-sm-12 col-xs-12 width-100 margin-45px-bottom xs-margin-25px-bottom\"><div class=\"blog-image\"><img width=\"1800\" height=\"1433\" src=\"https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_CGI_Hero-Image_©Bennetts-Associates-scaled.jpg\" class=\"attachment-full size-full wp-post-image\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" fetchpriority=\"high\" srcset=\"https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_CGI_Hero-Image_©Bennetts-Associates-scaled.jpg 1800w, https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_CGI_Hero-Image_©Bennetts-Associates-300x239.jpg 300w, https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_CGI_Hero-Image_©Bennetts-Associates-1024x816.jpg 1024w, https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_CGI_Hero-Image_©Bennetts-Associates-768x612.jpg 768w, https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_CGI_Hero-Image_©Bennetts-Associates-1536x1223.jpg 1536w, https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_CGI_Hero-Image_©Bennetts-Associates-2048x1631.jpg 2048w, https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_CGI_Hero-Image_©Bennetts-Associates-968x771.jpg 968w, https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_CGI_Hero-Image_©Bennetts-Associates-120x96.jpg 120w, https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_CGI_Hero-Image_©Bennetts-Associates-81x65.jpg 81w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1800px) 100vw, 1800px\" /></div></div><div class=\"col-md-12 col-sm-12 col-xs-12 blog-details-text entry-content\"><p><strong>A mixed-use office redevelopment, Timber Square comprises two significant buildings in Southwark’s Bankside area: the Print Building is a refurbished and dramatically extended former printworks; while the Ink Building is a 15-storey new timber-and-steel building.</strong></p>\n<div id=\"attachment_46205\" style=\"width: 588px\" class=\"wp-caption alignright\"><img decoding=\"async\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-46205\" class=\" wp-image-46205 lazyload\" src=\"data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAIBRAA7\" data-src=\"https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_Site-Photo_Aerial-View-2_©Heyne-Tillett-Steel-1024x610.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"578\" height=\"343\" /><p id=\"caption-attachment-46205\" class=\"wp-caption-text\"><noscript><img decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-46205 lazyload\" src=\"https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_Site-Photo_Aerial-View-2_©Heyne-Tillett-Steel-1024x610.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"578\" height=\"343\" srcset=\"https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_Site-Photo_Aerial-View-2_©Heyne-Tillett-Steel-1024x610.jpg 1024w, https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_Site-Photo_Aerial-View-2_©Heyne-Tillett-Steel-300x179.jpg 300w, https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_Site-Photo_Aerial-View-2_©Heyne-Tillett-Steel-1200x715.jpg 1200w, https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_Site-Photo_Aerial-View-2_©Heyne-Tillett-Steel-120x72.jpg 120w, https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_Site-Photo_Aerial-View-2_©Heyne-Tillett-Steel-81x48.jpg 81w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 578px) 100vw, 578px\" /></noscript> Aerial view of Timber Square site; © Heyne Tillett Steel</p></div>\n<p><strong>The Print Building: a new life for a 1950s printworks</strong><br />\nEighty percent of the 1950s printworks building was retained in the Print Building’s refurbishment and extension. It now has six additional storeys, achieved with minimal strengthening to the frame and foundations.<br />\n“Timber allowed us to really push that, because it’s so much lighter than using a composite concrete system,” explains Tom Watson, Director, Heyne Tillett Steel. “It helps that the building used to be a large print hall, designed for very high loads.”</p>\n<p><strong>The Ink Building: Europe’s tallest timber-and-steel office</strong><br />\nThe new-build part of Timber Square is the Ink Building. Like the Print Building, it is a hybrid structure using timber and steel. Its 15 storeys include a new double basement and piled raft foundations.<br />\nThe scheme creates new public realm space incorporating raingardens and a blue roof above its podium deck.</p>\n<p><strong>Keeping carbon down</strong><br />\n“The developers, Landsec, wanted to minimize embodied carbon, retain as much of the existing building as possible, and use the maximum amount of DfMA (design for manufacture and assembly),” Tom tells us. “We pitched a hybrid structure that uses long-span steel beams and plenty of CLT, while maximizing the height of the existing printworks building.”</p>\n<div id=\"attachment_46207\" style=\"width: 589px\" class=\"wp-caption alignright\"><img decoding=\"async\" aria-describedby=\"caption-attachment-46207\" class=\" wp-image-46207 lazyload\" src=\"data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAIAAAAAAAP///yH5BAEAAAAALAAAAAABAAEAAAIBRAA7\" data-src=\"https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_Site-Photo_Construction-1_©Heyne-Tillett-Steel-1024x768.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"579\" height=\"433\" /><p id=\"caption-attachment-46207\" class=\"wp-caption-text\"><noscript><img decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-46207 lazyload\" src=\"https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_Site-Photo_Construction-1_©Heyne-Tillett-Steel-1024x768.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"579\" height=\"433\" srcset=\"https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_Site-Photo_Construction-1_©Heyne-Tillett-Steel-1024x768.jpg 1024w, https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_Site-Photo_Construction-1_©Heyne-Tillett-Steel-300x225.jpg 300w, https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_Site-Photo_Construction-1_©Heyne-Tillett-Steel-768x576.jpg 768w, https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_Site-Photo_Construction-1_©Heyne-Tillett-Steel-1536x1152.jpg 1536w, https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_Site-Photo_Construction-1_©Heyne-Tillett-Steel-2048x1536.jpg 2048w, https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_Site-Photo_Construction-1_©Heyne-Tillett-Steel-1028x771.jpg 1028w, https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_Site-Photo_Construction-1_©Heyne-Tillett-Steel-120x90.jpg 120w, https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_Site-Photo_Construction-1_©Heyne-Tillett-Steel-81x61.jpg 81w, https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Timber-Square_Site-Photo_Construction-1_©Heyne-Tillett-Steel-scaled.jpg 1800w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 579px) 100vw, 579px\" /></noscript> Work in progress at Timber Square; © Heyne-Tillett Steel</p></div>\n<p>125 tonnes of reused steel was used across both buildings at Timber Square, sourced from Cleveland Steel &amp; Tubes: around 500 beams were used primarily in and around the buildings’ cores.<br />\n“Sitting CLT on top of steel beams allows you to install double-span 12-metre-long sections. You don&#8217;t have to stop them at every beam, so it’s a very efficient installation method. The CLT spans six metres in almost all cases, and the governing design criteria was footfall vibrations.&#8221;</p>\n<p>Developer: Landsec<br />\nArchitect: Bennetts Associates<br />\nStructural Engineer/Timber Engineer: <a href=\"https://timberdevelopment.uk/member-profile/heyne-tillett-steel-ltd/\">Heyne Tillett Steel</a><br />\nMain contractor: Mace<br />\nTimber supplier: <a href=\"https://timberdevelopment.uk/member-profile/stora-enso-uk-ltd/\">Stora Enso</a><br />\nTimber engineer: <a href=\"https://timberdevelopment.uk/member-profile/hybrid-structures-limited/\">Hybrid Structures</a></p>\n</div><div class=\"col-md-6 col-sm-12 col-xs-12 sm-text-center tag-cloud margin-20px-bottom\"> <a href=\"https://timberdevelopment.uk/tag/heyne-tillett-steel/\" rel=\"tag\">heyne tillett steel</a><a href=\"https://timberdevelopment.uk/tag/hybrid/\" rel=\"tag\">hybrid</a><a href=\"https://timberdevelopment.uk/tag/stora-enso-uk-ltd/\" rel=\"tag\">Stora Enso UK Ltd</a></div><div class=\"col-md-6 col-sm-12 col-xs-12 text-right sm-text-center pull-right pofo-post-detail-icon\"><ul class=\"extra-small-icon\"></ul></div><div class=\"col-md-12 col-sm-12 col-xs-12 no-padding pofo-related-posts\"><div class=\"col-md-12 col-sm-12 col-xs-12 margin-lr-auto text-center margin-80px-tb sm-margin-50px-tb xs-margin-30px-tb\"><div class=\"position-relative overflow-hidden width-100\"><span class=\"text-small text-outside-line-full alt-font font-weight-600 text-extra-dark-gray related-post-general-title\">RELATED ARTICLES</span></div></div><div class=\"equalize xs-equalize-auto\"><div class=\"col-md-4 col-sm-4 col-xs-12 last-paragraph-no-margin margin-50px-bottom sm-margin-50px-bottom xs-margin-30px-bottom wow fadeIn\"><div id=\"post-57105\" class=\"post-57105 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-build category-design category-supply tag-circular-building tag-climate-goals tag-design tag-grants tag-timber tag-woodstock tag-zero-waste news_themes-carbon news_themes-enviromental news_themes-esg news_themes-net-zero news_themes-products news_documents-article\"><div class=\"pofo-rich-snippet display-none\"><span class=\"entry-title\">€200,000 grant call to accelerate climate-smart wood construction  </span><span class=\"author vcard\"><a class=\"url fn n\" href=\"https://timberdevelopment.uk/author/jennie-ward/\">Jennie Ward</a></span><span class=\"published\">04 June 26</span><time class=\"updated\" datetime=\"2026-06-04T15:00:23+01:00\">04 June 26</time></div><div class=\"blog-post-style-related blog-post blog-post-style1 xs-text-center post-no-transform\"><div class=\"blog-post-images overflow-hidden margin-25px-bottom sm-margin-20px-bottom\"><a href=\"https://timberdevelopment.uk/e200000-grant-call-to-accelerate-climate-smart-wood-construction/\"><img width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" src=\"https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/woodstock-1024x768.jpg\" class=\"attachment-large size-large wp-post-image\" alt=\"\" title=\"\" decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/woodstock-1024x768.jpg 1024w, https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/woodstock-300x225.jpg 300w, https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/woodstock-768x576.jpg 768w, https://timberdevelopment.uk/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/woodstock-1536x