e-on-desktop menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-home menu-item-1150\"><a href=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/\">Start</a></li>\n<li id=\"menu-item-763\" class=\"menu-item menu-item-type-taxonomy menu-item-object-category menu-item-763\"><a href=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/./patterns/\">Patterns</a></li>\n<li id=\"menu-item-764\" class=\"menu-item menu-item-type-taxonomy menu-item-object-category current-post-ancestor current-menu-parent current-post-parent menu-item-764 current-menu-item\"><a href=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/./projects/\">Projects</a></li>\n<li id=\"menu-item-183\" class=\"menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-183\"><a href=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/pattern-theory/\">Theory</a></li>\n<li id=\"menu-item-27\" class=\"menu-item menu-item-type-post_type menu-item-object-page menu-item-27\"><a href=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/about/\">About</a></li>\n</ul></div>\t\t\t<!--Custom language toggle -->\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<ul class=\"nav-list nav-list--lang\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<!-- Set class for currently selected language -->\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"menu-item menu-item--lang\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/projects/crclr-house-berlin/\" class=\"current-lang\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\ten\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<!-- Set class for currently selected language -->\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"menu-item menu-item--lang\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/projekte/crclr-house-deutsch/\" class=\"\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\tde\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</a>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t</li>\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t</ul>\n\t\t\t\t\t</nav>\n\t</header>\n\n\t<main id=\"primary\" class=\"site-main\">\n\n\t\t\n<article id=\"post-672\" class=\"article post-672 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-projects\">\n\n\t<!-- 1. For patterns -->\n\t\n\t<!-- 2. For projects and all other post categories -->\n\t<!-- Content of Post -->\n\t<div class=\"entry-content\">\n\t\t\n<h1>CRCLR House: is a centre <br>for circular economy practices in the sectors <br>of construction, living <br>and community.</h1>\n\n\n\n<p>The CRCLR House is being built in a section of the former Kindl brewery in Berlin Neukölln. The existing warehouse is being extended by a modular wooden panel construction, so that the building can accommodate residential and commercial uses. The aim is to create living, working and commercial spaces in which materials are recycled in accordance with the principles of the Circular Economy. Likewise, during construction, attention will be paid to the recyclability of materials, or secondary building materials will be used and disassembly strategies will be considered. For example, resources were conserved by installing second-hand windows. As part of the initial use, the existing building was made usable again with only a few interventions and was available for temporary use as an event venue, coworking space and artist studio for the CRCLR community. As soon as the building is finalized, the Impact Hub Berlin will move in and offer co-working spaces, lab facilities and an event program.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/crclr-house-berlin-workshop-marlene-hildebrandt.jpeg\"><img width=\"1024\" height=\"682\" src=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/crclr-house-berlin-workshop-marlene-hildebrandt-1024x682.jpeg\" alt=\"Front view of the CRCLR house in Berlin\" class=\"wp-image-1836\" srcset=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/crclr-house-berlin-workshop-marlene-hildebrandt-1024x682.jpeg 1024w, https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/crclr-house-berlin-workshop-marlene-hildebrandt-300x200.jpeg 300w, https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/crclr-house-berlin-workshop-marlene-hildebrandt-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/11/crclr-house-berlin-workshop-marlene-hildebrandt.jpeg 1352w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" /></a><figcaption>Workshop on the construction site © Marlene Hildebrandt</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-container-2 wp-block-gallery-1 wp-block-gallery has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-construction-marlene-hildebrandt.jpeg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1024\" height=\"682\" data-id=\"1838\"  src=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-construction-marlene-hildebrandt-1024x682.jpeg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1838\" srcset=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-construction-marlene-hildebrandt-1024x682.jpeg 1024w, https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-construction-marlene-hildebrandt-300x200.jpeg 300w, https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-construction-marlene-hildebrandt-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-construction-marlene-hildebrandt.jpeg 1352w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" /></a><figcaption>Under construction © Marlene Hildebrandt</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-entrance-michael-prytula.jpeg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1024\" height=\"680\" data-id=\"1839\"  src=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-entrance-michael-prytula-1024x680.jpeg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1839\" srcset=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-entrance-michael-prytula-1024x680.jpeg 1024w, https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-entrance-michael-prytula-300x199.jpeg 300w, https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-entrance-michael-prytula-768x510.jpeg 768w, https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-entrance-michael-prytula.jpeg 1352w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" /></a><figcaption>Entrance and original façade of the CRCLR House © Michael Prytula</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-facade-elements-marlene-hildebrandt.jpeg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1024\" height=\"682\" data-id=\"1840\"  src=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-facade-elements-marlene-hildebrandt-1024x682.jpeg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1840\" srcset=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-facade-elements-marlene-hildebrandt-1024x682.jpeg 1024w, https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-facade-elements-marlene-hildebrandt-300x200.jpeg 300w, https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-facade-elements-marlene-hildebrandt-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-facade-elements-marlene-hildebrandt.jpeg 1352w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" /></a><figcaption>Reusable façade elements © Marlene Hildebrandt</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-hall-chantal-schoepp.jpeg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1024\" height=\"768\" data-id=\"1841\"  src=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-hall-chantal-schoepp-1024x768.jpeg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1841\" srcset=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-hall-chantal-schoepp-1024x768.jpeg 1024w, https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-hall-chantal-schoepp-300x225.jpeg 300w, https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-hall-chantal-schoepp-768x576.jpeg 768w, https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-hall-chantal-schoepp.jpeg 1352w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" /></a><figcaption>The hall before the reconstruction © Chantal Schöpp</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-second-level-marlene-hildebrandt.jpeg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1024\" height=\"682\" data-id=\"1842\"  src=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-second-level-marlene-hildebrandt-1024x682.jpeg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1842\" srcset=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-second-level-marlene-hildebrandt-1024x682.jpeg 1024w, https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-second-level-marlene-hildebrandt-300x200.jpeg 300w, https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-second-level-marlene-hildebrandt-768x512.jpeg 768w, https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-second-level-marlene-hildebrandt.jpeg 1352w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" /></a><figcaption>Second level in the existing building during the reconstruction © Marlene Hildebrandt</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><a href=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-reconstruction-marlene-hildebrandt.jpeg\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"682\" height=\"1024\" data-id=\"1843\"  src=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-reconstruction-marlene-hildebrandt-682x1024.jpeg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1843\" srcset=\"https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-reconstruction-marlene-hildebrandt-682x1024.jpeg 682w, https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-reconstruction-marlene-hildebrandt-200x300.jpeg 200w, https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-reconstruction-marlene-hildebrandt-768x1153.jpeg 768w, https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-reconstruction-marlene-hildebrandt-1023x1536.jpeg 1023w, https://www.buildingsocialecology.org/wp-content/uploads/2022/07/crclr-house-berlin-reconstruction-marlene-hildebrandt.jpeg 1352w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 682px) 100vw, 682px\" /></a><figcaption>In the hall during the reconstruction © Marlene Hildebrandt</figcaption></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<h2>General information</h2>\n\n\n\n<p></p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table is-style-regular\"><table class=\"has-black-color has-text-color\"><tbody><tr><td><strong>Architects</strong></td><td>Die Zusammenarbeiter GmbH</td></tr><tr><td>﻿</td><td>﻿</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Owner</strong></td><td><a href=\"https://www.trnsfrm.org/ueber-uns/\">TRNSFRM eG</a></td></tr><tr><td>﻿</td><td>﻿</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Address</strong></td><td>Rollbergstraße 26, 12053 Berlin</td></tr><tr><td>﻿</td><td>﻿</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Construction </strong><br><strong>period</strong></td><td>2019 &#8211; now (2021)</td></tr><tr><td>﻿</td><td>﻿</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Construction</strong></td><td>former warehouse is upgraded and supplemented with a <br>timber